{"duration": 43.267, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A coal miner carried a small bird deep underground.", "start": 0.05, "end": 2.397}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The bird rode in a cage, breathing faster than any man.", "start": 2.477, "end": 5.165}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The miner trusted this tiny creature with his life.", "start": 5.245, "end": 7.549}, {"beat": 1, "text": "The mine air could hide carbon monoxide, a gas with no smell.", "start": 7.749, "end": 10.778}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Miners could not see it, smell it, or feel it.", "start": 10.858, "end": 12.957}, {"beat": 1, "text": "It killed without warning.", "start": 13.037, "end": 14.253}, {"beat": 1, "text": "One breath of enough gas could stop a man's heart.", "start": 14.333, "end": 16.445}, {"beat": 2, "text": "You see, it's like a smoke detector beeping before you see flames.", "start": 16.645, "end": 19.483}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Canaries breathe faster and have a higher metabolism than miners.", "start": 19.683, "end": 22.625}, {"beat": 3, "text": "Their small bodies absorbed the poison first.", "start": 22.705, "end": 24.773}, {"beat": 3, "text": "The bird would collapse while the miners still felt fine.", "start": 24.853, "end": 27.179}, {"beat": 3, "text": "That collapse gave miners time to escape.", "start": 27.259, "end": 29.093}, {"beat": 3, "text": "The bird's distress was the alarm.", "start": 29.173, "end": 30.752}, {"beat": 4, "text": "John Scott Haldane proposed this idea in 1895.", "start": 30.952, "end": 34.045}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Canaries were used in mines as early as 1896.", "start": 34.125, "end": 36.96}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Modern sensors have replaced the birds.", "start": 37.04, "end": 38.916}, {"beat": 4, "text": "But the phrase 'canary in a coal mine' still warns us of hidden danger.", "start": 38.996, "end": 42.367}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.119, "end": 0.144, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "coal", "start": 0.194, "end": 0.344, "line": 0, "bea